w: O that my God would grant me grace To know and do His will!
w: Nor let my tongue in- dulge de- ceit, Nor act the li- ar's part.
w: Nor cov- et- ous de- sires a- rise With- in this soul of mine.
w: Let sin have no do- min- ion, Lord, But keep my con- science clear.
w: Yet since I've not for- got Thy way, Re- store Thy wand'r- ing sheep.
w: Nor let my head, or heart, or hands, Of- fend a- gainst my God.
